Hi,

On Thursday 27 October 2011, Mischa Vreeburg wrote:
> The version of the rkward package in the windows bundle is still 0.5.6 in
> the DESCRIPTION file.
> Is it still the 0.5.6 version or is the version nr not updated due to an
> oversite?

Yes, I simply forgot to bump the version number in the rkward R package.
Help->About RKWard should 0.5.7, correctly, and also the first line of 
rk.sessionInfo(). 

RKWard also checks the version of the rkward R package on each startup, so it 
will always load the package version that corresponds to the frontend (or show 
an error message). However, that check is not based on the version in the 
DESCRIPTION file for technical reasons (the "Version" field, there, does not 
permit some of the version names we use for testing releases).

Regards
Thomas
